      "side": 1,
      "message": "VMs seem to be working fine in my tests with crosvm. But I\u0027ve added some tracing here to see which leaves are enforced to different values by pKVM:\n```\n--- a/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/cpuid.c\n+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/cpuid.c\n@@ -1427,8 +1427,17 @@ static void kvm_enforce_cpuid_entry(struct kvm_cpuid_entry2 *entry,\n \t\tbreak;\n \t}\n \n-\tif (update)\n+\tif (update) {\n+\t\tif (memcmp(entry, \u0026tmp, sizeof(struct kvm_cpuid_entry2))) {\n+\t\t\tpr_info(\"pkvm: orig cpuid: func\u003d%x idx\u003d%x flags\u003d%x eax\u003d%x ebx\u003d%x ecx\u003d%x edx\u003d%x\\n\",\n+\t\t\t\tentry-\u003efunction, entry-\u003eindex, entry-\u003eflags, entry-\u003eeax, entry-\u003eebx,\n+\t\t\t\tentry-\u003eecx, entry-\u003eedx);\n+\t\t\tpr_info(\"pkvm:  new cpuid: func\u003d%x idx\u003d%x flags\u003d%x eax\u003d%x ebx\u003d%x ecx\u003d%x edx\u003d%x\\n\",\n+\t\t\t\ttmp.function, tmp.index, tmp.flags, tmp.eax, tmp.ebx,\n+\t\t\t\ttmp.ecx, tmp.edx);\n+\t\t}\n \t\t*entry \u003d tmp;\n+\t}\n }\n \n /*\n```\n\nAnd I have the following observations, for example on ADL:\n\n1. On some (not all) vCPUs, pKVM enforces different values of some cache parameters (functions 0x2, 0x4 and 0x80000006):\n\n```\n[  230.416961] pkvm: orig cpuid: func\u003d2 idx\u003d0 flags\u003d0 eax\u003dfeff01 ebx\u003df0 ecx\u003d0 edx\u003d0\n[  230.425248] pkvm:  new cpuid: func\u003d2 idx\u003d0 flags\u003d0 eax\u003dfeff01 ebx\u003d0 ecx\u003d0 edx\u003d0\n[  230.433418] pkvm: orig cpuid: func\u003d4 idx\u003d0 flags\u003d1 eax\u003d4121 ebx\u003d2c0003f ecx\u003d3f edx\u003d0\n[  230.442067] pkvm:  new cpuid: func\u003d4 idx\u003d0 flags\u003d1 eax\u003d4121 ebx\u003d1c0003f ecx\u003d3f edx\u003d0\n[  230.450718] pkvm: orig cpuid: func\u003d4 idx\u003d1 flags\u003d1 eax\u003d4122 ebx\u003d1c0003f ecx\u003d3f edx\u003d0\n[  230.459366] pkvm:  new cpuid: func\u003d4 idx\u003d1 flags\u003d1 eax\u003d4122 ebx\u003d1c0003f ecx\u003d7f edx\u003d0\n[  230.468016] pkvm: orig cpuid: func\u003d4 idx\u003d2 flags\u003d1 eax\u003d1c143 ebx\u003d240003f ecx\u003d7ff edx\u003d0\n[  230.476862] pkvm:  new cpuid: func\u003d4 idx\u003d2 flags\u003d1 eax\u003d1c143 ebx\u003d3c0003f ecx\u003d7ff edx\u003d0\n[  230.517974] pkvm: orig cpuid: func\u003d80000006 idx\u003d0 flags\u003d0 eax\u003d0 ebx\u003d0 ecx\u003d5007040 edx\u003d0\n[  230.526917] pkvm:  new cpuid: func\u003d80000006 idx\u003d0 flags\u003d0 eax\u003d0 ebx\u003d0 ecx\u003d8008040 edx\u003d0\n```\n\nAnd AFAICS crosvm actually sets native values of those leaves (it executes the CPUID instruction to obtain them).\n\nSo, I believe, those cache parameters are different on different CPU cores, whereas pKVM enforces the same values (which it obtained once during bootup, on one CPU) for all vCPUs, regardless on which CPU the given vCPU is running. Seems like a problem?\n\n(Of course crosvm\u0027s setup is also not 100% correct in this regard, since a vCPU may migrate to a different CPU at runtime. But that\u0027s not the point.)\n\n2. On all vCPUs, pKVM enforces different values of some FPU params (according to SDM, those params are \"Maximum size (bytes, from the beginning of the XSAVE/XRSTOR save area) required by\nenabled features in XCR0\" and \"supported bits of the lower 32 bits of the IA32_XSS MSR\"):\n\n```\n[  230.485715] pkvm: orig cpuid: func\u003dd idx\u003d0 flags\u003d1 eax\u003d207 ebx\u003d240 ecx\u003da88 edx\u003d0\n[  230.493979] pkvm:  new cpuid: func\u003dd idx\u003d0 flags\u003d1 eax\u003d207 ebx\u003da88 ecx\u003da88 edx\u003d0\n[  230.502230] pkvm: orig cpuid: func\u003dd idx\u003d1 flags\u003d1 eax\u003df ebx\u003d240 ecx\u003d0 edx\u003d0\n[  230.510102] pkvm:  new cpuid: func\u003dd idx\u003d1 flags\u003d1 eax\u003df ebx\u003d348 ecx\u003d0 edx\u003d0\n```\n\nI haven\u0027t analyzed if it is ok that pKVM changes these values. So, is it ok?\n\n3. On all vCPUs, pKVM enforces KVM PV features enumerated in KVM_CPUID_FEATURES:\n```\n[  230.535860] pkvm: orig cpuid: func\u003d40000001 idx\u003d0 flags\u003d0 eax\u003d0 ebx\u003d0 ecx\u003d0 edx\u003d0\n[  230.544217] pkvm:  new cpuid: func\u003d40000001 idx\u003d0 flags\u003d0 eax\u003d1007efb ebx\u003d0 ecx\u003d0 edx\u003d0\n```\n\nSeems not quite correct, since we don\u0027t really support those KVM features for pVMs (although probably harmless, since pVM will not try to use those features anyway, since KVM_CPUID_SIGNATURE is set to PKVMPKVMPKVM instead of KVMKVMKVM).\n\n4. Also if I run a VM with `--host-cpu-topology`, pKVM for some reason enforces the \"Core type\" value to zero, instead of the correct native value set by crosvm (0x40 \u003d \"Intel Core\" for P-cores, 0x20 \u003d \"Intel Atom\" for E-cores):\n\n```\n[ 7161.292958] pkvm: orig cpuid: func\u003d1a idx\u003d0 flags\u003d0 eax\u003d20000001 ebx\u003d0 ecx\u003d0 edx\u003d0\n[ 7161.292960] pkvm:  new cpuid: func\u003d1a idx\u003d0 flags\u003d0 eax\u003d0 ebx\u003d0 ecx\u003d0 edx\u003d0\n[ 7161.292961] pkvm: orig cpuid: func\u003d1a idx\u003d0 flags\u003d0 eax\u003d40000001 ebx\u003d0 ecx\u003d0 edx\u003d0\n[ 7161.292963] pkvm:  new cpuid: func\u003d1a idx\u003d0 flags\u003d0 eax\u003d0 ebx\u003d0 ecx\u003d0 edx\u003d0\n```\n\nI have no idea why this happens.",
      "revId": "d61fe9755076eea43145357b6cf2e8bd378e2a73",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
