      "writtenOn": "2025-10-29T21:43:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Finally got to testing it on PTL... It doesn\u0027t work well: I\u0027m hitting this -EINVAL here, so pKVM-high reports `Failed to set cpuid pages for pkvm vcpu` errors, and VMs fail to start.\n\nThe problematic unknown leaf is the following one:\n\n```\n[   22.989251] pkvm_enforce_cpuid: unknown leaf: func\u003d4 idx\u003d4 flags\u003d1 eax\u003d0 ebx\u003d0 ecx\u003d0 edx\u003d0\n```\n\nSo, some cores have 4 levels of caches, while others have only 3. So this is a similar observation to the one we\u0027ve been discussing in another comment, but in this case the CPUID entry not just has a different value from the one in `pkvm_hyp-\u003ecpuid_def` but is simply missing in `pkvm_hyp-\u003ecpuid_def`.\n\nI\u0027ve tried replacing `return -EINVAL` with `memset(\u0026e2[i], 0, sizeof(struct kvm_cpuid_entry2))` here, and now it appears to work fine.\n\nIf we apply this fix, then, echoing my question from the other comment: I hope it won\u0027t be a problem if the pVM will think there is no L4 cache (or, depending on luck, the other way around: if it will wrongly think there are L4 caches on all cores)?",
      "revId": "d61fe9755076eea43145357b6cf2e8bd378e2a73",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
